r what you pay for compared to other middle eastern food places in IV. I liked my beef shawarma. He liked his chicken shawarma. We were both happy. Once we found out this place closed we were both in despair. Nothing lasts forever I guess :'(\\\\n\\\\nREST IN KEBAB MAGIC PITA 2014. YALL BE MISSED\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2014-04-06 19:18:48\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":3.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Basic mediterranean nothing special here. Points for being after midnight go-to. Owner is a nice dude, Kilo or Phylo or something. Staff b.s. around with each other (talk, laugh) so orders take longer than they would if they were concentrating. Seems to attract a more ghetto late night crowd than the Blue Owl & I'm sure being right next to a smoke shop (hookah shop? Don't know I didn't go in) helps with that. Mad amounts of Taxis park in front so unless you like shady looking mexican dudes staring at you while you grub get it to go. Not much room to eat inside, never tried it.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2014-03-21 04:03:28\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":2.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"I wanted to like this place because I truly enjoy Middle Eastern cuisine and there is not much choice in that category here in Santa Barbara.  Unfortunately, I will not be going back for more food from the Magic Pita Cafe.  There was way, way too much garlic used in many of the dishes; I got sick from it, not to mention the resultant bad breath.  The water-logged salad was loaded with onion- more b.b.  The meat was overcooked. And the servers neglected to include pita bread in my order which I discovered only after I got home.  A sad disappointment.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Here is an objective overview of the Magic Pita Cafe based on the structured data provided:\\n\\nThe Magic Pita Cafe is a Restaurant located in Santa Barbara, California, offering Middle Eastern and Mediterranean cuisine. The cafe has a rating of 4.0 stars and is open from 11:30 AM to 3:00 AM, seven days a week. The business provides outdoor seating and WiFi, but does not offer reservations or validation for parking. The atmosphere is casual and welcoming, with no live music or ambiance features listed.\\n\\nReviews for the cafe are mixed, with some customers praising the quality and value of the food, particularly the beef and chicken shawarma. However, others have complained about the garlic content in some dishes, leading to discomfort and bad breath. Additionally, some reviewers have noted that the service can be slow and inconsistent, with long wait times and incorrect orders. Overall, the Magic Pita Cafe seems to offer decent Middle Eastern cuisine, but may need to improve its service and menu options to meet customer expectations.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
