r Ferrari race winner Fernando Alonso finished his first race for the McLaren Honda partnership with 12th place in China. The Spanish double world champion missed the Australian Grand Prix because of a head injury sustained in testing and then retired in Malaysia.\\n\", \"answer\": \"Lewis Hamilton won his 35th grand prix at the Chinese Grand Prix, leaving his teammate Nico Rosberg unhappy with his performance. The Mercedes driver claimed that Rosberg had ruined his race by driving too slowly. The championship standings show that Hamilton has a lead of 13 points over Ferrari's Sebastian Vettel, with Rosberg just four points behind him. The German driver expressed his frustration after the race, claiming that Hamilton's slow driving had hindered his progress. The next race will take place in Bahrain, where Rosberg hopes to turn things around and make a comeback.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n", "add_special": true}
