uted to this report.\\n\", \"answer\": \"Two shootings occurred in Washington, D.C., with authorities stating they were connected. The shootings started with a domestic kidnapping incident, and a guard at the U.S. Census Bureau was shot when approaching the suspect's vehicle. The suspect fled and a chase ensued, ending in a shootout and leaving an officer and the suspect injured. The police chief believes the same car and person were involved in the kidnapping. The victim was found and in good condition. The identities of those involved were not disclosed.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
