oasting pan from the oven and test to make sure the duck is finished cooking. 1  Insert a cooking thermometer into the thickest portion of the duck meat, either the breast or thigh. 2  Be sure the thermometer is not touching any bones.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to cook a duck in the oven\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to cook a duck in the oven:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 400 degrees F ( passage 2).\\n2. Season the entire duck breast with essence (passage 2).\\n3. Heat a cast iron skillet or other oven-safe skillet over medium heat (passage 3).\\n4. Place the duck legs in the pan with the skin sides down (passage 3).\\n5. Cook the duck legs until the skin is brown, about 3 minutes (passage 3).\\n6. Place the pan in the oven (passage 3).\\n7. Roast the duck in the preheated oven for 1 hour (passage 1).\\n8. Spoon 1/4 cup melted butter over the duck and continue cooking for an additional 45 minutes (passage 1).\\n9. Rub salt, pepper, and paprika into the skin of the duck (passage 1).\\n10. Remove the roasting pan from the oven and test to make sure the duck is finished cooking (passage 3).\\n\\nNote: The passages do not specify the size of the duck or the desired level of doneness, so the cooking time may need to be adjusted accordingly.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
