 bipartisanship credentials,\u201d wrote Indivisible Bucks County in a news release that pointed out the congressman\u2019s support for a national abortion ban, school book bans and the GOP\u2019s \u201csham committee to amplify conspiracy theories and discredited witnesses.\u201d\\nJordan, the founding member of the right-wing House Freedom Caucus , is alleged to have first-hand knowledge of events surrounding the January 6 insurrection and defied a Jan. 6 Committee subpoena for testimony and documents. An outspoken support of Donald Trump, Jordan has also refused to acknowledge that President Joe Biden won the 2020 election.\\n\u201cOver a dozen other Republicans had the courage to vote against Representative Jordan for Speaker, and Fitzpatrick chose to vote for Donald Trump\u2019s choice instead of joining his more principled colleagues,\u201d said Kierstyn Zolfo of Indivisible Bucks County.\\nReactions on Twitter (X) to Fitzpatrick\u2019s Support for Jim Jordan :\", \"answer\": \"Here is a summary of the article in 92 words:\\n\\nBucks County Rep. Brian Fitzpatrick voted to elect Jim Jordan as Speaker of the House, despite criticism from his Democratic opponent and indivisible groups. Fitzpatrick has been touted as a moderate, but his support for Jordan, a far-right Republican, raises questions about his political courage and values.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
