er takes turns rolling all 6 dice. If no point dice appear (a Farkle), the player loses any points collected during that turn and play passes to the left. If the player chooses not to risk rolling a Farkle, they can stop rolling and record their points on the scratch paper. Points are awarded for sets of three of a kind (2,500 points), four of a kind (1,000 points or double/quadruple three of a kind value), and five of a kind (2,000 points or triple/six times three of a kind value). The objective is to have the highest score after 10 rounds of play.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
