ng of the year, often because of bad weather and overcrowded vessels used by smugglers, the IOM said. Sometimes the captains and crews abandon the ships, leaving passengers to fend for themselves. Last week: 978 migrants rescued in one day in Mediterranean Sea. CNN's Ralph Ellis contributed to this report.\\n\", \"answer\": \"A total of 8,480 migrants were rescued off the coast of Italy from Friday to Monday, according to the Italian coast guard. The coast guard also received SOS calls from 20 boats in distress on Monday. However, 'Save the Children' fears that 400 migrants could be missing after a ship carrying 550 people capsized in the Mediterranean Sea. The Italian coast guard is taking the report seriously, though it has found no evidence to confirm the incident.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
