bank nor her social media accounts. Further, there's no indication of her contacting friends or family or leaving the country. Importantly, Detective Peterson highlighted that Delly is an immigrant from Haiti.\\nIn a startling twist, the Naples Daily News reported that Dareus moved to Orlando shortly after Marie\u2019s disappearance. The same publication also highlighted that Dareus was convicted in 2015 for first-degree murder with a firearm, linked to the fatal shooting of Hyatt Regency employee Cedilien Forestal in Orlando.\\nEvery piece of information can be pivotal. If you know anything about Marie Chantal Delly or the ongoing investigation, please assist by calling the Collier County Sheriff\u2019s Office at (239) 252-9300. And remember, if you're more comfortable remaining anonymous, Crime Stoppers is ready to listen at (800) 780-TIPS (8477).\", \"answer\": \"Marie Chantal Delly, a mother of four from Florida, disappeared mysteriously after finishing her shift at Walmart in 2010. She was last seen leaving the store and has not been heard from since. Her husband, Mathnauld Dareus, is a person of interest due to inconsistencies in his account and has since moved to Orlando. There is a reward for any information leading to Delly's whereabouts.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
