4.48.305.075 D srv  log_server_r: request:  {"model": "unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-GGUF", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Judge whether any answer claim is unsupported by the complete source. Return only JSON with p_hallucination (0 to 1), quote (one verbatim source string of at most 32 words, or null), byte_start and byte_end (half-open UTF-8 byte offsets, or null). A quote is evidence to inspect, not an entailment certificate. Do not use external knowledge. Input JSON follows:\n{\"source\": \"{\\\"passages\\\":\\\"passage 1:Communicable disease refers to diseases that can pass from one person to another. Non-communicable diseases occur in one person and cannot be passed on to another person. Communicable diseases are also known as infectious diseases, and non-communicable diseases are referred to as chronic.\\\\n\\\\npassage 2:One important difference between communicable and non-communicable disease is that non-communicable diseases tend to be chronic, which means they last a long time and progress slowly. Communicable diseases are more likely to be acute, which means the disease develops quickly.\\\\n\\\\npassage 3:Cancers are one category of non-communicable diseases that cannot be spread to others. Chicken pox and other conditions caused by viruses are communicable diseases. Non-infectious diseases involving the respiratory system are a class of non-communicable conditions.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"what is the difference between communicable and non communicable diseases\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Communicable diseases can be passed from one person to another, while non-communicable diseases cannot be transmitted. Communicable diseases are often acute and caused by viruses, while non-communicable diseases are chronic and can last a long time. Some examples of communicable diseases are chicken pox, while non-communicable diseases include cancers and respiratory system conditions.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cac