netic testing before you have children.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"what are some reasons genetic testing is done\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Genetic testing is done to identify changes in chromosomes, genes, or proteins. The results can confirm or rule out a suspected genetic condition or help determine a person\u2019s chance of developing or passing on a genetic disorder. Genetic testing is often done if a person has symptoms of a disease that may be caused by genetic alterations, or if they have a family history of a genetic disorder. It can also be done if a person is in an ethnic group that has a high risk of a particular genetic disorder. Additionally, early genetic screening can be an important step in planning for a healthy family, particularly if one or both parents are carriers of a genetic disease.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
