ould possibly contaminated with Covid. It will be a long time before I ever go back. Pretty sad on the owner's part not to be enforcing basic sanitary guidelines. Plus who knows when this young man last sanitized his hands. Even sadder is that they lost my order of the day and many other future orders. \\\\nRoughly $150 worth of business in cold cuts and multiple sandwiches...\\\\nConsumers beware of these sad and pathetic health practices.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-05-03 22:21:35\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":4.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"It's tough to find a meal under 10$ in this town. But Nona's delivers. If you're looking for a classic no nonsense Italian sub, this place hits the spot! Also, Michelle is very friendly! Will definitely be revisiting for lunch.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2021-04-06 04:42:26\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":1.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Dried up and barren. The entire deli looks like it was created as a movie set or like a fake grocery store in North Korea. Don't waste your time there. what kind of Italian deli sells top ramen\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Nona's Italian Deli is a local business located at 415 E De La Guerra St in Santa Barbara, CA. It falls under various categories, including Restaurants, Sandwiches, Specialty Food, Pasta Shops, Grocery, Food, Ethnic Grocery, and Delis. The deli operates from Monday to Friday, between 11:00 AM and 2:00 PM, offering its customers a limited time frame to enjoy their meals.\\n\\nThe business has received mixed reviews from customers. One customer expressed disappointment with the lack of adherence to basic sanitary guidelines during the COVID-19 pandemic. They observed an employee not wearing a face mask properly, which raised concerns about the potential contamination of the food. This incident led the customer to reconsider visiting the deli in the future.\\n\\nOn the other hand, another customer praised Nona's for providing affordable meals, with an Italian sub being highlighted as a standout item. The customer also appreciated the friendly service provided by Michelle.\\n\\nOne negative review criticized the appearance of the deli, describing it as dried up and barren, comparing it to a movie set or a fake grocery store in North Korea. The customer advised others not to waste their time at Nona's and questioned the authenticity of an Italian deli selling top ramen.\\n\\nOverall, Nona's Italian Deli has received a 3.0-star rating, indicating a mixed customer experience. It is known for its affordability and classic Italian subs, although some customers have raised concerns about sanitation and the overall ambiance of the deli.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
