\\"hipster\\\":false,\\\"intimate\\\":false,\\\"romantic\\\":false,\\\"touristy\\\":false,\\\"trendy\\\":false,\\\"upscale\\\":false},\\\"BusinessParking\\\":{\\\"garage\\\":false,\\\"lot\\\":false,\\\"street\\\":true,\\\"valet\\\":false,\\\"validated\\\":false},\\\"Music\\\":null,\\\"OutdoorSeating\\\":false,\\\"RestaurantsGoodForGroups\\\":false,\\\"RestaurantsReservations\\\":true,\\\"RestaurantsTakeOut\\\":true,\\\"WiFi\\\":\\\"no\\\"},\\\"business_stars\\\":3.5,\\\"categories\\\":\\\"Wine Bars, Restaurants, American (New), Nightlife, Seafood, Cocktail Bars, Bars\\\",\\\"city\\\":\\\"Santa Barbara\\\",\\\"hours\\\":{\\\"Friday\\\":\\\"12:0-23:0\\\",\\\"Monday\\\":\\\"0:0-0:0\\\",\\\"Saturday\\\":\\\"11:0-23:0\\\",\\\"Sunday\\\":\\\"11:0-22:0\\\",\\\"Thursday\\\":\\\"12:0-22:0\\\",\\\"Tuesday\\\":\\\"12:0-22:0\\\",\\\"Wednesday\\\":\\\"12:0-22:0\\\"},\\\"name\\\":\\\"The Hungry Cat\\\",\\\"review_info\\\":[{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2016-11-29 07:26:22\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":2.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Dropped in here after the good reviews, but was disappointed by a bad oyster shucker (took way too long and contained many shell chunks) and mediocre to good food. Octopus was over-salted, but green salad was great. Lobster was good. \\\\n\\\\nIn their defense, perhaps, the waitress did apologize for how long our oysters took. She explained that the shucker was new and politely implied he didn't know what he was doing, which left me wondering why he was shucking oysters at a seafood restaurant. \\\\n\\\\nSome good things: the space is great, modern without being too formal or drab. Our waitress was obviously good, though challenged by a difficult kitchen and bar (one glass of wine was forgotten). \\\\n\\\\nOverall, this felt like a place with a lot of potential in need of better leadership in the kitchen.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2016-11-16 00:03:40\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":1.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Knowing it was late for dinner, we checked ahead and made a reservation for 8 at 9:00 pm.  When we arrived, we were told the restaurant was closing but they would check with the chef and see if he wanted to stay.  We said we'd made a reservation and then we started hearing about what a busy weekend they'd had but they'd check on the reservation -- as we watched the chef leave through the front door.  Then we were told they were out of many items due to earlier business.\\\\n\\\\nSince we didn't get to eat, I can't comment on the food.  I later heard that the restaurant is under new management -- if this is true, I'd suggest some intensive staff training.\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2016-11-11 01:42:10\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":2.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Really not pleased with the visit tonight. I've had so much better from this place in the past. We had a hair in out fries.Nuff said.\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Sure! Here's an objective overview of The Hungry Cat based on the provided structured data:\\n\\nThe Hungry Cat is a Wine Bar and Restaurant located in Santa Barbara, CA, with a rating of 3.5 stars based on customer reviews. The menu offers American New cuisine, Seafood, Cocktail Bars, and Nightlife. The restaurant has a modern atmosphere without being too formal or drab, and the outdoor seating area is available for guests to enjoy. However, there have been some issues with the kitchen and service, as some reviews mention a bad oyster shucker, over-salted octopus, and forgetfulness in serving drinks. Additionally, some reviewers noted that the restaurant was understaffed and disorganized. Despite these issues, the restaurant has potential and offers great salads and lobster. Reservations are accepted, and Wi-Fi is not available.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
