ing a platform for multinationals to challenge domestic laws. Warren warned in a December letter that the TPP could erode safeguards against future financial crises. Obama has dismissed Warren's concerns, causing some consternation among Democratic voters. Meanwhile, presidential hopeful Hillary Clinton is trying to straddle both sides of the debate. During her tenure as Secretary of State, Clinton praised the TPP as the \\\"gold standard\\\" in trade agreements. However, she has recently echoed Warren's populist rhetoric and refused to definitively state her position on the TPP.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n"}
