0 mph.\\nAs the colossal waves generated by the force of Bolaven began their journey towards the California coast, surfers and thrill-seekers around the region knew that Maverick's was on the cusp of an unforgettable day.\\nSuper Typhoon Bolaven may have brought havoc and destruction in its wake, but it also gifted California's most famous big wave spot with an unforgettable day of surfing.\\nIt was a reminder that in the world of big wave riding, when the call of the ocean beckons, those who heed it are rewarded with an experience like no other.\", \"answer\": \"On October 18, surfers and thrill-seekers flocked to California's Maverick's surf spot as Super Typhoon Bolaven generated massive waves up to 18 feet high. The Mav's crew, known for their dedication to big wave riding, waste no time responding to the ocean's call. Super Typhoon Bolaven rapidly intensified from a category one to a category five hurricane, unleashing winds of up to 180 mph and generating waves that rewarded surfers with an unforgettable experience.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
