ea on April 27. CNN's Paula Hancocks contributed to this report.\\n\", \"answer\": \"Sure! Here's the summary in 70 words:\\n\\nSouth Korea's Prime Minister Lee Wan-koo offered to resign amid a political scandal over alleged bribery and corruption. Seven politicians, including Lee and those linked to President Park Geun-hye, are under investigation. Lee denies allegations, but the President is taking them seriously and has promised to root out corruption.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
