uctureisto place the ledger board at the correct height, horizontal and level with the roof.The ledger board should be fastened securely in place with wall bolts or lag screws. 2  Reinforce with flashing.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to attach a ledger board to a house for a patio cover\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, here are the steps to attach a ledger board to a house for a patio cover:\\n\\n1. Determine the correct height for the ledger board: Measure the height of the soffit board above the sliding glass door to determine where the ledger board should be positioned. Make sure the ledger board is level and horizontal with the roof.\\n2. Install wall bolts or lag screws: Use wall bolts or lag screws to secure the ledger board to the house. Drill a pilot hole through the ledger board and into the rim joist of the house, then insert a lag screw and washer. Tighten the screw with a socket wrench.\\n3. Cut flashing strips: Cut equal strips of waterproof self-adhering membrane and metal flashing the length of the ledger board and 6 inches wide.\\n4. Attach the flashing: Apply the flashing strips to the ledger board, starting from the bottom and working upwards. Ensure the flashing is secured tightly to the ledger board and overlaps the edges of the board.\\n5. Reinforce with additional flashing: Add additional flashing strips at the eaves and rake edges of the roof to ensure proper drainage and protection against water intrusion.\\n\\nPlease note that the passages do not provide specific instructions for attaching the ledger board to the two posts on the opposite side of the patio. It is assumed that these details will be addressed in subsequent passages or separate instructions.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n", "add_special": true}
