e house. Drill a pilot hole through the ledger board and into the rim joist of the house, then insert a lag screw and washer. Tighten the screw with a socket wrench.\\n3. Cut flashing strips: Cut equal strips of waterproof self-adhering membrane and metal flashing the length of the ledger board and 6 inches wide.\\n4. Attach the flashing: Apply the flashing strips to the ledger board, starting from the bottom and working upwards. Ensure the flashing is secured tightly to the ledger board and overlaps the edges of the board.\\n5. Reinforce with additional flashing: Add additional flashing strips at the eaves and rake edges of the roof to ensure proper drainage and protection against water intrusion.\\n\\nPlease note that the passages do not provide specific instructions for attaching the ledger board to the two posts on the opposite side of the patio. It is assumed that these details will be addressed in subsequent passages or separate instructions.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
