. Gram-negative bacteria are often harmful to a host, which is the case for many of the Salmonella bacteria.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"salmonella bacteria characteristics\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Salmonella bacteria are rod-shaped, non spore-forming, motile microbes. They have thin cell walls and are gram-negative. They are between 2 and 5 micrometers long and 0.7 to 1.5 micrometers in diameter. They have flagella, which are tail-like projections made of proteins that help the bacteria to move. There are more than 2,000 different serotypes of Salmonella, but Salmonella Enteritidis and Salmonella Typhimurium cause more than 50% of human infections.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
