\\"It would not be proper to cast aspersions on Pakistan's commitment to countering terrorism at a time when Pakistan has entered a critical stage of defeating the menace of terrorism.\\\" The Foreign Office also blamed what it said was India's delay in cooperating in the case, saying it \\\"weakened the prosecution.\\\" In the Mumbai attacks, heavily armed men stormed landmark buildings around Mumbai, including luxury hotels, the city's historic Victoria Terminus train station and a Jewish cultural center. India executed the last surviving gunman from the attacks in 2012. Other suspects were all killed during the series of attacks, which went on for three days. More about the Mumbai attacks. CNN's Harmeet Singh contributed to this report.\\n\", \"answer\": \"Zaki-ur-Rehman Lakhvi, a top leader of the terrorist group Lashkar-e-Taiba, was released on bail in Pakistan after years of detention. Lakhvi was charged with masterminding the 2008 Mumbai terror attacks that left over 160 people dead. India has condemned Lakhvi's release, accusing Pakistan of having a \\\"dual policy\\\" on dealing with terrorists. Pakistan's Foreign Office responded, blaming India's delay in cooperating with the case and weakening the prosecution. The release of Lakhvi has highlighted the long-running tensions between India and Pakistan, who have had three wars since their partition.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n", "add_special": true}
