 regular cast iron pan. Start with high quality steaks, choice grade or better like a center cut, be it a filet, rib eye, or strip steak. With marbling, the white ribbons of fat running through the beef.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to cook flank steak indoors\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, here's how to cook flank steak indoors:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 250\u00b0F (200\u00b0C).\\n2. Season the flank steak with salt and pepper.\\n3. Place the steak on a rack over a baking sheet.\\n4. Roast the steak in the center of the oven for about 20 minutes, or until it reaches medium-rare.\\n5. Remove the steak from the oven and heat oil in a medium skillet over high heat.\\n6. Add the steak to the skillet and sear until it's deep brown and crisp, about 3 minutes per side.\\n7. Hold the steak on its sides and cook the edges for 1 minute per side.\\n8. Return the steak to the rack and let it rest for 10 minutes.\\n9. Slice the steak against the grain and serve.\\n\\nSo, the answer is: Preheat oven to 250\u00b0F, season the steak, place it on a rack, roast in the oven, sear in a skillet, and rest before slicing and serving.\"}"}], "add_generation_prompt": true, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
