ng blue or showing a bluish tinge due to lack of oxygen.\\n4. Pain, tingling, or a feeling of pins and needles as blood flow returns to the affected area.\\n5. The symptoms can be triggered by exposure to cold temperatures, stress, or other factors.\\n\\nIt is important to note that these symptoms can also be caused by other conditions, so a proper diagnosis by a medical professional is necessary to confirm Raynaud's disease.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
