 instances \\\"coercive\\\" and \\\"high-risk,\\\" instead of \\\"unsafe and unprofessional.\\\" Ratner, Pentagon spokesperson, did not reveal the basis for these two designations.\\nNavy Adm. John Aquilino, the acclaimed chief of U.S. Indo-Pacific Command, has expressed worries about the risks of flying off one's wing for 45 minutes at 15 feet. Adm. Aquilino warned that such activities could cause accidents.\\nThe Pentagon released declassified photographs and videos of UAP events recently. The Pentagon calls these disturbing images \\\"reckless maneuvers, close approaches at high speeds in the air, releasing objects and projectiles like flares, and other dangerous behavior.\\\" These documents try to reveal the mysterious encounters that have baffled specialists for years.\\nAdmiral John Aquilino, director of the U.S. Indo-Pacific Command, said the Pentagon has observed Chinese military clashes. Aquilino believes these attacks are part of a Chinese military strategy. The discovery highlights rising US-China Indo-Pacific tensions.\\nRecent reports suggest Defense Secretary Lloyd Austin has been privately discussing their dealings with China. Austin discussed this with Chinese officials, according to Department of Defense spokesperson Emily Ratner. The nature and details of these exchanges are unknown.\\nEdited by Newsbreak Contributor Denys Shybinskiy\", \"answer\": \"The Pentagon has released secret photos and videos of encounters between US and Chinese aircraft, highlighting the escalating tensions between the two nations. The visuals show Chinese fighter jets engaging in \\\"coercive\\\" and \\\"high-risk\\\" behavior, including close approaches and releases of objects at high speeds. The US hopes the release of these images will increase transparency and awareness of the situation. Experts have noted a significant increase in such encounters in recent years, with over 180 instances since September 2021. The Pentagon has labeled some interactions as \\\"unsafe\\\" and \\\"unprofessional,\\\" while others have been described as \\\"coercive\\\" and \\\"high-risk.\\\" Navy Adm. John Aquilino, head of US Indo-Pacific Command, has expressed concern about the risks of such encounters, warning that they could lead to accidents.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
