 FBI. Traces of blood were found inside the vehicle, further supporting the theory that Jiminez may have committed the crime in the car before moving the body to the bathtub, per FBI officials.\\nInvestigators stated they suspect that Jiminez's brother might have driven him to Mexico in the same vehicle and left him there. Since the night of the wedding, Jiminez has managed to elude authorities and remains unaccounted for. FBI officials believe he is likely in hiding in Mexico, specifically in the Santiago Papasquiaro area or in Reynosa, Tamaulipas.\\nA $250,000 reward is being offered for information leading to Jimenez's arrest, per officials.\\nFBI officials also stated that Jimenez should be considered armed and dangerous. If you have any information concerning this person, please call 1-800-CALL-FBI or contact your nearest American Embassy or Consulate.\", \"answer\": \"The FBI has added Arnaldo Jiminez, a 41-year-old man, to its Top 10 Most Wanted list due to serious charges in Texas. He is accused of stabbing his newlywed wife, Estrella Carrera, to death in her Baton Rouge apartment two years ago. A $250,000 reward is being offered for information leading to his arrest, and the FBI considers him armed and dangerous.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n"}
