gerator. 2  Season meat as desired. 3  Place seasoned meat in an uncovered roasting pan on a shelf in the bottom 1/3 of your oven. 4  Bake EXACTLY 5 1/2 minutes PER POUND. 5  Adjust +/- according to your oven's accuracy and heat retention. 6  NOTE:.\\\\n\\\\npassage 2:Swirl to coat the bottom. Roast the pork for 10 minutes: Set the pork in the pan. (It's fine if your pork tenderloin is a little long for the pan; just bend it to fit as we did here.) Return the pan to the oven. Roast for 10 minutes.Flip the pork, reduce the heat, and roast another 10 to 15 minutes: Flip the pork to the other side.oast the pork for 10 minutes: Set the pork in the pan. (It's fine if your pork tenderloin is a little long for the pan; just bend it to fit as we did here.) Return the pan to the oven. Roast for 10 minutes.\\\\n\\\\npassage 3:1 Preheat oven to 500 degrees. 2  Remove tenderloin from refrigerator. 3  Season meat as desired. 4  Place seasoned meat in an uncovered roasting pan on a shelf in the bottom 1/3 of your oven. 5  Bake EXACTLY 5 1/2 minutes PER POUND. 6  Adjust +/- according to your oven's accuracy and heat retention.7  NOTE:. Remove tenderloin from refrigerator. 2  Season meat as desired. 3  Place seasoned meat in an uncovered roasting pan on a shelf in the bottom 1/3 of your oven. 4  Bake EXACTLY 5 1/2 minutes PER POUND. 5  Adjust +/- according to your oven's accuracy and heat retention. 6  NOTE:.\\\\n\\\\n\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"how to cook thin pork tenderloin in oven with foil\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the given passages, here's how to cook a thin pork tenderloin in the oven with foil:\\n\\nPreheat the oven to 500 degrees. Season the pork tenderloin as desired. Place the seasoned meat in an uncovered roasting pan on a shelf in the bottom 1/3 of the oven. Bake EXACTLY 5 1/2 minutes PER POUND. Adjust the cooking time +/- according to your oven's accuracy and heat retention.\\n\\nAfter 10 minutes, remove the pork tenderloin from the oven and lightly cover it with foil. Let it rest for 5-10 minutes to redistribute the internal juices. The roast should be done, slightly pink in the center, and very moist. After resting 10 minutes, the roast should reach a safe internal temperature of 145-150 degrees.\\n\\nTherefore, to cook a thin pork tenderloin in the oven with foil, you should follow these steps:\\n\\n1. Preheat the oven to 500 degrees.\\n2. Season the pork tenderloin as desired.\\n3. Place the seasoned meat in an uncovered roasting pan on a shelf in the bottom 1/3 of the oven.\\n4. Bake EXACTLY 5 1/2 minutes PER POUND.\\n5. Adjust the cooking time +/- according to your oven's accuracy and heat retention.\\n6. Cover the pork tenderloin with foil after 10 minutes of cooking.\\n7. Let it rest for 5-10 minutes to redistribute the internal juices.\\n8. Check the internal temperature of the roast, which should be 145-150 degrees after resting 10 minutes.\"}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
