zing concept!  We are using the truck again this year as it has been such a hot item!!\\\"},{\\\"review_date\\\":\\\"2017-07-31 03:14:02\\\",\\\"review_stars\\\":5.0,\\\"review_text\\\":\\\"Mario was freaking amazing !!!! He was so charismatic and instinctful !! He's defiantly a one man show !! I would refer him for any event !! He bartender my friend Pilar wedding and did a amazing job !!!\\\"}],\\\"state\\\":\\\"CA\\\"}\", \"answer\": \"Based on the provided passages, the main differences between the two-toed sloth (Choloepus didactylus) and the three-toed sloth (Bradypus variegatus) are:\\n\\n1. Number of toes on the front limbs: The two-toed sloth has two toes on each front limb, while the three-toed sloth has three toes.\\n2. Size: The two-toed sloth is generally smaller than the three-toed sloth, with a length of around 23-27 inches (58-68 cm) and a weight of around 17.5-18.75 pounds (about 8 kilograms), compared to the three-toed sloth's length of around 30-40 inches (76-102 cm) and weight of around 20-30 pounds (around 9-14 kilograms).\\n3. Limb structure: The two-toed sloth has longer limbs overall, with the forelegs being slightly longer than the hind legs, while the three-toed sloth has shorter forelegs that are 35% longer than the hind legs.\\n4. Hand structure: The two-toed sloth has hands with two functioning fingers and sharp claws, while the three-toed sloth has three fingers on its hands.\\n5. Vertebral count: The two-toed sloth has six or seven vertebrae in its body, while the three-toed sloth has nine vertebrae.\\n6. Tail length: The three-toed sloth has a smaller tail than the two-toed sloth.\\n7. Forelimb length: The three-toed sloth has substantially longer forelegs than the rear legs, while the two-toed sloth has more balanced proportions.\"}"}], "temperature": 0, "top_p": 1, "seed": 70553, "max_tokens": 128, "cache_prompt": false, "chat_template_kwargs": {"enable_thinking": false}}
